WEBVTT

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:03.459
Previously on Smallville.

00:00:03.459 --> 00:00:04.459
How many times do I have to apologize?

00:00:04.459 --> 00:00:06.459
I don't want an apology!

00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:08.460
The hell were you so afraid of.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.460
You.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.460
It'll be okay, Tommy. I promise.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.460
How can you do this to me? Just stay away!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.460
I want to introduce you to some people, a sort of team.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.460
We'll make a hero out of you yet.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.460
Let's deserve to die, Chloe.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.460
This is murder.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.460
You know what I did was right.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.460
You can't help Clark.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.460
I would do anything for you.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.460
Let's leave Smallville.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.460
Where are you?

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.460
Chloe!

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:50.659
I said no.

00:00:50.659 --> 00:00:52.659
We can't risk the casualties, okay?

00:00:52.659 --> 00:00:54.659
You wait for the team to move in.

00:00:54.659 --> 00:01:04.540
Well, you seem to be taking my open-door policy

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.540
a little liberally these days, don't you?

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.540
I guess I assumed after you ambushed me in my barn

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.540
and accused me of being an alien Jesus that we had dropped any formalities.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.299
Yeah, I can't say that the Sarcalis.

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:18.299
I can't say that the sarcasm adds to your coy charm.

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:21.299
But please, come in.

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:23.299
Greasy Kung Powell for one?

00:01:23.299 --> 00:01:25.299
I don't have much of an appetite.

00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:27.299
Okay, then. Tell me.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:29.299
What's on your mind, Clark?

00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:32.299
Do you really think that spreading panic is responsible journalism?

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:35.299
Making Davis Bloom front-page news every day is reckless.

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:37.299
Reckless?

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:44.150
I think reckless is not doing everything in your power to stop him.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:47.150
Starting a massive man on his

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.150
isn't helping anyone.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:52.150
Clark, if you don't want to admit your true identity, that's fine.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:56.150
But we both know that Davis Bloom isn't a man.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:02:01.390
He's a beast.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:06.390
If he is this beast, then encouraging the police to go after him is dangerous.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.390
People will die.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:11.389
And when that happens, you'll know where to find him

00:02:11.389 --> 00:02:21.819
so that you can finally slay the proverbial dragon.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:23.819
This is not some fairy tale.

00:02:23.819 --> 00:02:25.819
Obviously, there's some dark part of you that needs to be

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:27.819
be saved, but I'm not your white knight.

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:29.819
You're risking innocent lives, including Chloe's.

00:02:29.819 --> 00:02:31.819
All right.

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:33.819
The accomplice of the serial killer.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:36.819
She's his hostage, and she's in the most danger.

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:39.819
If you're so worried about her getting hurt,

00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:44.479
why are you fighting my help?

00:02:44.479 --> 00:02:47.479
Maybe it's because you're actually afraid to find Davis.

00:02:47.479 --> 00:02:53.680
Because the pure and virtuous Clark Kent

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.960
can't face what he'll have to do,

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.960
what you're destined to do when that moment comes.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:11.939
Clark.

00:03:11.939 --> 00:03:12.939
Clark.

00:03:12.939 --> 00:03:16.939
I'm just making sure you embrace the inevitable.

00:03:16.939 --> 00:05:45.430
I really should get you to the hospital, Chloe.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:06:07.670
I understand if you don't want to talk about it.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:13.129
He never left me alone.

00:06:13.129 --> 00:06:17.129
There was this motel just outside Metropolis that we found,

00:06:17.129 --> 00:06:20.129
and he wouldn't let me leave.

00:06:20.129 --> 00:06:44.050
We're so scared.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:46.050
We just hid during the day until dark,

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.050
and then...

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.050
One day he decided...

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:54.779
he decided that it was time to leave.

00:06:54.779 --> 00:06:56.779
And so we stopped at this gas station.

00:06:56.779 --> 00:07:09.139
I just ran.

00:07:09.139 --> 00:07:10.139
You're safe now.

00:07:10.139 --> 00:07:17.850
No, Clark. He's still out there.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.850
Anything that was good in him.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:23.730
No one's safe.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:45.629
You'd destroy that piece.

00:07:45.629 --> 00:07:47.629
I can't believe we lost track of that thing.

00:07:47.629 --> 00:07:50.629
If I had their powers, I would have gotten the job down.

00:07:50.629 --> 00:07:53.629
They're the ones that strewed up.

00:07:53.629 --> 00:07:54.629
No one else.

00:07:54.629 --> 00:07:59.509
So quick to assign blame.

00:07:59.509 --> 00:08:02.500
I taught you to take care of one of one of us.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.500
you to take care of one another.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.500
You were trained as a team.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.500
If one of you fails, then all of you fail.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.500
What the hell is going on here?

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:15.480
Livewire and Neutron found the monster.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:18.480
By the time, Parasite and I showed up.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:20.480
Things had gotten messy.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:23.480
She said Neutron zapped him with some sort of radioactive blast.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:28.480
Your mission was to find him and then wait until I sent the traveler.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.480
Is that all you can think about?

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:33.480
Neutron's dead!

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.480
Hey!

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.480
Back off.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.480
Tess was trying to keep us safe.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.480
It was you and Neutron who didn't wait for backup.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:43.480
That thing cut us tailing him, and he attacked.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:46.480
We didn't have a chance!

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.480
I am not going to be the opening act to this traveler

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:51.480
when you won't even clue us into who it is.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.480
I want out!

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.480
So you can go back to stealing cars and running from the cops?

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.480
Tess turned your life around.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:02.480
Give us a place where we belonged.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.480
A chance to do something good.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.480
to do something good for the world.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:09.480
We all suffered a loss here,

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.480
but we should learn a lesson from this.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:15.049
We're only strong when we're together.

00:09:15.049 --> 00:09:19.049
If we find that beast, you will save so many lives.

00:09:19.049 --> 00:09:22.049
You can't walk away from that.

00:09:22.049 --> 00:09:24.049
Watch me.

00:09:24.049 --> 00:09:46.759
Go find another sucker to be your hero.

00:09:46.759 --> 00:09:47.759
Thanks for the power up.

00:09:47.759 --> 00:09:57.279
It's up to you two now to find him.

00:09:57.279 --> 00:09:59.279
Don't worry.

00:09:59.279 --> 00:10:01.279
We won't let you down.

00:10:01.279 --> 00:10:09.190
So what are you going to do?

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:10.190
with me now?

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:12.190
Put me back in jail?

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:27.279
Cyborg, Impulse and Canary.

00:10:27.279 --> 00:10:29.279
I have a wide net out for Davis so far.

00:10:29.279 --> 00:10:31.279
They haven't caught anything.

00:10:31.279 --> 00:10:32.279
Where's Chloe?

00:10:32.279 --> 00:10:34.279
Something happened.

00:10:34.279 --> 00:10:37.279
I can't believe I put her through something like this again.

00:10:37.279 --> 00:10:39.279
First Brainiac and now, Davis.

00:10:39.279 --> 00:10:41.279
It's not even over yet.

00:10:41.279 --> 00:10:42.279
He's still out there.

00:10:42.279 --> 00:10:45.279
Something tells me without his beauty to soothe the beast.

00:10:45.279 --> 00:10:47.279
Not much time.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:52.230
Davis may not be as invincible as we thought.

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:53.230
There is something that might work.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:58.379
There's something that might work, but I can't do it alone.

00:10:58.379 --> 00:11:01.379
Yeah, it means getting rid of this guy once and for.

00:11:01.379 --> 00:11:03.379
I'll just say the word I'm in.

00:11:03.379 --> 00:11:04.379
Good.

00:11:04.379 --> 00:11:06.379
Because we're going to need the help of Lex Luthor.

00:11:06.379 --> 00:11:14.600
Clark, last time I heard, Lex Luthor was in no-conditional end-to-hand.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:17.600
When Lex was murdered, he left all his kryptonian research to test Mercer.

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:19.600
Meteor rocks, crystals, and artifacts.

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:21.600
She keeps them all in a safe.

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:24.600
I think she has something that might work on Davis.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:25.600
It's black kryptonite.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:31.919
I need you to steal it.

00:11:31.919 --> 00:11:33.919
Because if there's meteor rock in there,

00:11:33.919 --> 00:11:38.029
kill you. I get it.

00:11:38.029 --> 00:11:42.029
Well, it's been a while, but I could probably find my way into the Ice Queen's vault.

00:11:42.029 --> 00:11:45.029
Thank you. I knew I could count on you.

00:11:45.029 --> 00:11:47.029
That's never going to change.

00:11:47.029 --> 00:11:58.519
Believe me, I know how difficult this is. We're supposed to be the good guys.

00:11:58.519 --> 00:12:00.519
But sometimes you have to get our hands dirty.

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:02.519
Do what's necessary.

00:12:02.519 --> 00:12:07.370
It's the only option.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:41.139
We need to kill Davis-Bloon.

00:12:41.139 --> 00:12:43.139
What are you doing with the crystal?

00:12:43.139 --> 00:12:45.139
Look, Chloe.

00:12:45.139 --> 00:12:47.139
Don't worry about it, okay? I don't want you involved. You've been there.

00:12:47.139 --> 00:12:49.139
I don't want you involved. You've been through enough already.

00:12:49.139 --> 00:12:55.159
Clark, I just survived a gothic romance with Dr. Jackal and Mr. Hyde.

00:12:55.159 --> 00:12:59.889
I think I can handle anything you throw at me.

00:12:59.889 --> 00:13:01.889
I'm going to save Davis.

00:13:01.889 --> 00:13:03.889
What?

00:13:03.889 --> 00:13:06.889
When did you plan on telling me this?

00:13:06.889 --> 00:13:09.889
I wasn't going to tell you till after I took care of it.

00:13:09.889 --> 00:13:12.889
Clerk, you told me that you sent Oliver on a mission

00:13:12.889 --> 00:13:15.889
to find your own brand of Kryptonian hemlock.

00:13:15.889 --> 00:13:20.580
I lied. I don't know, Chloe.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.580
It seems like in order to do the right thing lately

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:24.580
there has to build these lies and secrets attached.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:27.580
I didn't even know if Oliver would help me if I told him the truth.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:30.820
Which is?

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.820
My parents once used black kryptonite night to split off my kryptonian side.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:41.860
I'm going to separate Davis from the Beast and use this crystal to send doomsay to the phantom zone.

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:43.860
Spare me the kryptonian mumbo-jumbo.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:45.860
You have to bend the rules on this one.

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:50.860
When I took Davis to the fortress, you stopped me from sending him away.

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.860
You knew he was worth saving.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:53.860
I was wrong.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:58.740
No, you weren't wrong, Chloe.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:00.740
I know what you've been through, but there's still a side of David.

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:01.740
It's human.

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:06.080
So then what if the plan fails?

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.799
It won't.

00:14:09.799 --> 00:14:13.659
Sometimes justice.

00:14:13.659 --> 00:14:18.259
It's not about making the easy decision.

00:14:18.259 --> 00:14:23.259
Sometimes it's about finding that last bit of good in someone and saving them from themselves.

00:14:23.259 --> 00:14:27.009
You taught me that.

00:14:27.009 --> 00:14:39.700
What is it?

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:54.789
It's from Dr. Emile. Jim Zay struck again.

00:14:54.789 --> 00:14:57.789
John Jones gave me the heads up when Granville police got the call.

00:14:57.789 --> 00:15:01.789
He's stalling local authorities, but we have to move fast.

00:15:01.789 --> 00:15:03.789
Bonespur embedded six inches into concrete.

00:15:03.789 --> 00:15:06.789
concrete? You're right, because they did make an appearance.

00:15:06.789 --> 00:15:08.789
Unfortunately, he had an audience.

00:15:08.789 --> 00:15:10.789
A man and a woman both dead.

00:15:10.789 --> 00:15:12.789
Clark, we have to stop him before he kills more innocent people.

00:15:12.789 --> 00:15:14.789
Maybe they weren't so innocent.

00:15:14.789 --> 00:15:16.789
They were both meteor-infected.

00:15:16.789 --> 00:15:19.789
And from the evidence we've gathered, it looks like they were hunting him.

00:15:19.789 --> 00:15:22.789
Right. Now that Test made Davis public enemy number one,

00:15:22.789 --> 00:15:24.789
we have supercharged bounty hunters on the case.

00:15:24.789 --> 00:15:27.789
Who died doing what they believed was right?

00:15:27.789 --> 00:15:28.789
Maybe.

00:15:28.789 --> 00:15:31.789
But I think something else is going on here.

00:15:31.789 --> 00:15:32.789
Two victims died from very different.

00:15:32.789 --> 00:15:54.500
very different causes.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:55.500
She's been marked.

00:15:55.500 --> 00:16:00.700
You sure the beast killed her?

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:02.700
That's not a mark on her body.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:06.809
It's because he didn't kill her.

00:16:06.809 --> 00:16:08.809
This did.

00:16:08.809 --> 00:16:11.809
It's a temporal lobe implant.

00:16:11.809 --> 00:16:14.809
GPS device. It's also a small explosive.

00:16:14.809 --> 00:16:16.809
I don't know what triggered it.

00:16:16.809 --> 00:16:18.809
When it went off, it killed her.

00:16:18.809 --> 00:16:20.809
It was blown into her ear canal where I found it.

00:16:20.809 --> 00:16:23.809
Someone other than Doomsday wanted her dead.

00:16:23.809 --> 00:16:25.809
Someone who was controlling her.

00:16:25.809 --> 00:16:29.980
And monitoring her.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:31.980
Chloe, you okay?

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:34.980
Yeah, I think all the mayhem is just a little more than I can handle.

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:37.980
I'm gonna go outside for some fresh air.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:38.980
But, Chloe?

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:40.980
Look, I don't like you going outside alone.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:42.980
Not when Doomsay could be so nearby.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:43.980
Clark, it's just outside.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.980
Trust me, if he comes back, I'll holler.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:56.190
I know all that she's been through must be taking its toll.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:59.190
But I think something else is going on with her.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:01.190
Why would you say that?

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:05.190
The feelings for Davis Bloom may be stronger than she's telling you.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.190
Last week,

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:08.190
She came to me desperate to cure him.

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:11.569
She didn't tell me that.

00:17:11.569 --> 00:17:13.569
That's not surprising, Clark.

00:17:13.569 --> 00:17:18.910
When it comes to affairs of the heart,

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:21.910
everyone uses secrets and lies to protect the ones they love.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:44.619
I bet I think we have a serious problem.

00:17:44.619 --> 00:17:46.619
You guys were there. You must have seen what happened.

00:17:46.619 --> 00:17:49.619
It ticked me off that she screwed up the job.

00:17:49.619 --> 00:17:52.619
But all I did to Live Wire was Hoover Powers.

00:17:52.619 --> 00:17:54.619
Yeah. When we left,

00:17:54.619 --> 00:17:56.619
a Scarity Cat had all nine lives.

00:17:56.619 --> 00:17:58.619
I know it wasn't us. That's the point.

00:17:58.619 --> 00:18:03.619
There was an explosive microchip in her brain that landed her in a body bag.

00:18:03.619 --> 00:18:06.619
Look, I'm sorry she's history. What's it got to do with us?

00:18:06.619 --> 00:18:08.619
We're wasting time.

00:18:08.619 --> 00:18:11.619
She'd be hunting down Godzilla before he tears down Metroportar.

00:18:11.619 --> 00:18:13.619
Don't you get it? Tess put that thing in her head.

00:18:13.619 --> 00:18:16.619
I'm starting to wonder if we can believe anything she's said.

00:18:16.619 --> 00:18:20.619
Look, Tess kept us out of jail in Belle Rive.

00:18:20.619 --> 00:18:24.619
She pays for our room, our ride, and our three squares a day.

00:18:24.619 --> 00:18:26.619
She gave me the home I never had.

00:18:26.619 --> 00:18:28.619
And she did a lot more for you.

00:18:28.619 --> 00:18:32.619
When everybody else turned their backs on us, she was there.

00:18:32.619 --> 00:18:34.619
I don't want to believe it either.

00:18:34.619 --> 00:18:37.619
But after all the tests and procedures we had at Black Creek,

00:18:37.619 --> 00:18:39.619
I mean, who's to say we're not chipped right now?

00:18:39.619 --> 00:18:42.619
Do you know how long it took for Tess to put this team together?

00:18:42.619 --> 00:18:45.619
Why would she ice one of us in cold blood?

00:18:45.619 --> 00:18:48.619
She's done us too many solids to do something like that.

00:18:48.619 --> 00:18:52.619
Somebody else pulled the plug on live wire, not Tess.

00:18:52.619 --> 00:18:59.789
Come on. We're finishing this job, just like we promised her.

00:18:59.789 --> 00:19:19.039
Your secretary said you were out.

00:19:19.039 --> 00:19:22.039
Your assignment was to insult your new business partner.

00:19:22.039 --> 00:19:23.039
Eat an A-plus.

00:19:23.039 --> 00:19:25.039
And you flung to getting the hint.

00:19:25.039 --> 00:19:29.380
I don't have time for a wine tasting, Oliver.

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:33.380
Corporate titans need to learn how to multitask, Tess.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:36.859
It's all business.

00:19:36.859 --> 00:19:38.859
That's not a quarterly earnings report.

00:19:38.859 --> 00:19:40.859
You're always very perceptive.

00:19:40.859 --> 00:19:42.859
You know I like that in a woman.

00:19:42.859 --> 00:19:45.859
It's a turn on.

00:19:45.859 --> 00:19:47.859
If I remember correctly,

00:19:47.859 --> 00:19:50.859
when it comes to the opposite sex,

00:19:50.859 --> 00:19:53.390
there's little that.

00:19:53.390 --> 00:20:00.160
doesn't turn you on.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:02.160
Actually, there's only been one woman that ever had that effect.

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:05.500
Nice try.

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.500
